think The mesh IS the validator set: the three demo nodes that vouch are exactly the roll enrolled, so a real quorum is judged against the real roll it belongs to. The crux — two tools, one answer: the app rebuilds the Dag under cord.add, gathers a three-node quorum over the genesis-funded account, confirms the roll passes it (pass_muster), and emits the position tuple bc7cbcb5… 100 100 200; the independent statement_dag_truth.awk names the identical position (app.out == awk.out enforced).
